{"hash":"fee06cae6518136e","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":91.57,"said":"Nandi sits here, patient, facing his Lord. Patience is what this part of the story needs. Gautama’s disciples went to the water with their pots, but the other sages’ wives turned them away: ‘We draw first.’ So Ahalya went herself, calmly made peace, and brought the water home. The wives were offended, and told their husbands a twisted tale. The angry sages prayed to Ganesha to drive Gautama out. Ganesha warned them: ‘He saved you from starving. To harm him is wrong, and it will turn against you.’ They insisted, and Ganesha, who cannot refuse his devotees, agreed. He took the form of a weak, staggering cow and wandered into Gautama’s field of grain. Gautama, gentle by nature, shooed it away with a few blades of grass, and the cow fell dead. At once the hidden sages cried out, ‘Gautama has killed a cow!’ They drove him out with stones. Gautama asked humbly how he could atone. Walk around Brahmagiri, they told him, bring the Ganga here, and worship a crore of earthen lingas. And so, with Ahalya beside him, he began. Now climb up into the hall, to see what that devotion brought.\n\nDid you know? Circling Brahmagiri on foot is still a pilgrimage here; the old temple establishment even kept two men whose duty was to walk the mountain’s parikrama.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1091},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1107,"end":1258}],"words":[[0.098,0.433,0,5],[0.543,0.3,6,10],[0.855,0.325,11,15],[1.348,0.565,17,24],[2.141,0.421,26,32],[2.574,0.228,33,36],[2.814,0.373,37,41],[4.051,0.505,43,51],[4.567,0.144,52,54],[4.724,0.24,55,59],[4.976,0.18,60,64],[5.168,0.288,65,69],[5.469,0.084,70,72],[5.565,0.096,73,76],[5.673,0.397,77,82],[6.082,0.445,83,88],[7.416,0.721,90,99],[8.149,0.649,100,109],[8.81,0.3,110,114],[9.123,0.084,115,117],[9.219,0.096,118,121],[9.327,0.409,122,127],[9.748,0.132,128,132],[9.892,0.156,133,138],[10.06,0.457,139,143],[10.745,0.12,145,148],[10.877,